JohnWAlbright wrote:
>
> Help for a newb

Go ahead and write it out.  There's no call for dork-speak abbreviations
on UseNet.  There is, however, call for acronyms on UseNet.  Cultures
vary.

> Food Poisoning

Some foods are poisonous.  Some can grant poison resistance.  Some do
both.  Some do neither.  Four possibilities.  Learn which of the 4
possible slots each corpse falls into until you have gotten the message
that tells you you are now immune to poison.

> Gnomish Mines (great place to get some good equipment but usually too tough)

Be less agressive.  Be more ready to retreat.  I often take 5-6 attempts
before I clean out the first level and I don't descend father until then.
Before then I am always ready to flee back up the stairs and wander the
main dungeon until ready.  I also do a level of mines and a level of main
dungeon until I've found the enterance to Sokoban and mines end.

> Wererats (lycanthropy stinks)

Learn about magical cancellation and MC=3 armor types.  Throw more
missiles.

> running out of food

Hunters go deeper into the bush and they eat what they kill.  If you
survive the mines you're unlikely to encounter this later.  Plenty of
food in the process of cleaning out every level of the mines.

Also, never go burdened.  It costs more food in addition to combat
problems.

> generally running into monster that kick my butt and ruin all my fun.

Run away.  Use corridors to face them one at a time.  Run away.  Throw
more missiles.  Run away up the stairs.  Let your pet run interference
in addition to letting it fight.

